section_context[12]:
  - title: "Cold Chain and Yard Safety"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/cold-chain-safety/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "A container drifts warm overnight and nobody opens the door until morning. What the yard camera already sees, read against the handover record and the paperwork the consignment travels with."
  - title: "Customer Data Privacy and Emissions Reporting"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/compliance/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "Operating a system quietly writes personal data into its own logs, and the emissions report takes a quarter to assemble. What the software reads for each, what it hands to the person accountable, and where a check it could not run says so."
  - title: "Freight Claims and Port Charges"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/claims-recovery/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "Claims expire because assembling one takes a morning. The entry, the hold, the missing documents, the days held and the per-day charge arrive already gathered and joined, so a person only has to judge whether the case holds."
  - title: "Re-Running the Route After the Day Has Changed"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/route-optimization/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "The plan that was optimal at six in the morning is not optimal by ten. Nobody re-runs it, because re-running it means re-planning a day by hand. This is about making the second run cost nothing."
  - title: "Returns and What to Do With Them"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/responsive-reverse-logistics/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "A returned item is worth the most on the day it comes back. The call on where it goes — shelf, refurbishment, recycling or disposal — is drafted at the scan, from a written-down policy that gives the same grade the same answer every time."
  - title: "Stock Cover and Supplier Planning"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/fulfillment-optimization/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "Most stockout warnings arrive after the safety stock is already gone, which leaves you paying for air freight. The point is to see it while there is still time to order normally."
  - title: "Talking to Drivers Without a Screen"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/voice-dispatch/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "The person who knows a load is late is the one who cannot type. Asking and answering out loud gets the fact onto the record while the truck keeps moving, and the desk still makes the change."
  - title: "Testing a Plan Before You Commit to It"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/hypothesis-lab/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "A port shuts and you have a day to pick a new route. State the change as a hypothesis and the rules it touches, and get back the case laid out — which rules it collides with, in what order, and what someone would have to believe for the plan to hold. The decision stays with the person accountable for it."
  - title: "The Picture Nobody Has Time to Assemble"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/supply-chain-visibility/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "The facts are in four systems in four formats, and joining them takes a morning nobody has. So the picture that would let somebody act only ever gets assembled after the fact, for the meeting that reviews it."
  - title: "When Demand Turns Before the Plan Does"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/demand-forecasting/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "A line starts moving weeks before the reorder point does. By the time the plan catches up the cover is gone, and the difference is paid in air freight. This is about reading the turn while it is still a forecasting problem."
  - title: "Which Clause Governs This, and Who Checked"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/paralegal-review/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "A routine question settled by a paragraph takes a day and a half to answer, so it gets answered from memory instead. The clause and the record arrive together, cited. The reading is the software's. The judgement is not."
  - title: "Your Adjusters Spend the Day Gathering, Not Deciding"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/use-cases/insurance-underwriting/"
    date: "2024-05-20T00:00:00Z"
    description: "The policy wording, the loss report, the reserve history and the authority limit for a claim that size sit in four places. They arrive joined, with a drafted next step and the reading it rests on. The underwriter still decides."
